      <widget class="QLabel" name="gsdModeLabel">
       <property name="font">
        <font>
         <pointsize>10</pointsize>
        </font>
       </property>
       <property name="toolTip">
        <string>How ADIAT converts real-world track sizes into pixels.
Every setting below is in centimeters on the ground, so the ground sample distance (GSD) of each image must be known.
• From Image Metadata: calculated per image from the drone's altitude and camera data (recommended)
• Fixed Value: the same GSD is used for every image
If an image has no usable altitude/camera metadata, the fixed value is used for it instead.
Over steep terrain the altitude above takeoff can differ from the height above the snow; use a fixed value if you know the true GSD.</string>
       </property>
       <property name="text">
        <string>GSD Source:</string>
       </property>
      </widget>
     </item>
     <item>
      <widget class="QComboBox" name="gsdModeComboBox">
       <property name="font">
        <font>
         <pointsize>10</pointsize>
        </font>
       </property>
       <property name="toolTip">
        <string>Where the ground sample distance (cm per pixel) of each image comes from.
• From Image Metadata: calculated from altitude and camera data, falling back to the fixed value
• Fixed Value: always use the fixed value</string>
       </property>
       <item>
        <property name="text">
         <string>From Image Metadata</string>
        </property>
       </item>
       <item>
        <property name="text">
         <string>Fixed Value</string>
        </property>
       </item>
      </widget>
